IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsea-employment`

-- National Servicemen (Employment) Act 1970, ss 4 to 10 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_national-servicemen-employment-act-1970.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`unregistered hire under an order, no consent` MEANS Hiring WITH
    `an order under section 5 is in force` IS TRUE
    `the order covers the employer` IS TRUE
    `the order covers this kind of employee` IS TRUE
    `the order excepts these circumstances` IS FALSE
    `the employer must take the person on by written law` IS FALSE
    `the employer must take the person on by a pre-1971 agreement` IS FALSE
    `the person is a registered person` IS FALSE
    `the Director consented in writing` IS FALSE

